    "result_text": "The full suite is green (1 test file, `AcceptanceTest`, passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner GET response to expose an `initials` field \u2014 the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nChanges, kept to small cohesive additions with no growth to existing methods:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema, alongside the existing `displayName`. The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the initials inline, mirroring the existing `displayName` mapping:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java((owner.getFirstName().charAt(0) + \\\".\\\" + owner.getLastName().charAt(0) + \\\".\\\").toUpperCase())\")\n   ```\n\nThis adds the behaviour as a declarative mapping (CC 1) rather than touching any procedural method, and follows the established `displayName` pattern already in the codebase. `mvnw test` reports `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
